{% comment %}
  Renders a GoKwik "Buy Now" button for the shared product card.

  Accepts:
  - card_product: {Object} Product Liquid object (required)
  - section_id: {String} The ID of the section that contains this card (used for aria wiring)

  Renders nothing unless settings.goEnable AND settings.goCardBuynowEnable are on
  and the selected/first available variant is purchasable. Products that need the
  quick-add modal (multiple variants / quantity rules) additionally require
  settings.goBuynowEnable, because the modal's Buy Now button comes from the
  fetched PDP buy-buttons block.

  Notes (intentional GoKwik vendor coupling — see snippets/gokwik.liquid):
  - The <card-buy-now> wrapper carries the `gokwik-checkout` class ON PURPOSE:
    the vendor glue in gokwik.liquid enables every `.gokwik-checkout button`
    after the `gokwikLoaded` window event (and keeps re-enabling them via a
    body-wide MutationObserver, which also covers Owl clones / fetched cards),
    and the international flow hides `.gokwik-checkout` for non-India visitors.
  - Never use id "gokwik-buy-now" here — the vendor targets that single ID for
    the PDP Buy Now button.
  - The FIRST CHILD of the button must be the loader element (.addloadr, hidden
    inline); the vendor sets id="btn-loader" on children[0] while the checkout
    screen loads. It contains Dawn's loading-spinner.svg (instead of the vendor
    .cir-loader) so the loader matches the add-to-cart button's default spinner;
    component-card-buy-now.css shows it when the button is :disabled with the
    id applied.
  - Behavior lives in assets/card-buy-now.js; styles in assets/component-card-buy-now.css.
    Both are loaded site-wide from layout/theme.liquid when the feature is enabled,
    because related-products/search inject cards via innerHTML (scripts emitted
    with the cards would never execute there).

  Usage:
  {% render 'card-buy-now', card_product: card_product, section_id: section_id %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign variant = card_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign needs_modal = false
  if card_product.variants.size > 1 or variant.quantity_rule.min > 1 or variant.quantity_rule.max != null or variant.quantity_rule.increment > 1
    assign needs_modal = true
  endif
  assign render_buy_now = false
  if settings.goEnable and settings.goCardBuynowEnable and card_product != blank and variant.available
    assign render_buy_now = true
  endif
  comment
    The modal path relies on the PDP Buy Now button (settings.goBuynowEnable +
    dynamic checkout in buy-buttons.liquid) being present in the fetched
    quick-add modal. Without it the modal would be a mislabeled dead end,
    so skip rendering entirely for products that need the modal.
  endcomment
  if needs_modal and settings.goBuynowEnable != true
    assign render_buy_now = false
  endif
-%}
{%- if render_buy_now -%}
  <card-buy-now
    class="card-buy-now gokwik-checkout"
    data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}"
    data-product-url="{{ card_product.url }}"
    {% if needs_modal %}
      data-modal="#QuickAdd-{{ card_product.id }}"
    {% endif %}
    {% if settings.hideFlow %}
      style="display:none !important;"
    {% endif %}
  >
    <button
      type="button"
      class="button card-buy-now__btn disabled"
      disabled
      id="CardBuyNow-{{ section_id }}-{{ card_product.id }}"
      aria-labelledby="CardBuyNow-{{ section_id }}-{{ card_product.id }} title-{{ section_id }}-{{ card_product.id }}"
    >
      <div style="display:none" class="addloadr" aria-hidden="true">
        {{- 'loading-spinner.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </div>
      <span>{{ settings.cardBuynowText | default: 'Buy Now' | escape }}</span>
    </button>
  </card-buy-now>
{%- endif -%}
